# moldingFoam::postSolve sum over the boundary patches, so their
# reductions must not sit inside the loop (a decomposed mesh has a
# different number of processor patches on each rank). The case runs
# twice in run-solver-tests.sh: serially and, because system/nProcs
# exists, in parallel over the asymmetric decomposition declared in
# system/decomposeParDict. Under the defect the parallel pass deadlocks
# inside the first postSolve (bounded by the harness timeout).
moldingFoam: filling
moldingFoam: mass budget patch
End
